45,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
48,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
49,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The candidates are A: Textiles, B: Maritime, C: City Excavation, and D: Light and Motion. I lean toward A.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"A and C both offer the human element visitors love. However, C involves a conservation bench.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, a conservation bench sounds great, but I found the lab is totally overwhelmed! C is too much work.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"D has kinetic works, which means powered displays. My research says those break too often. I'm out on D.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"B involves loans from partner collections, which means high transport costs and risky paperwork. A is much leaner.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"A uses local craftspeople for demonstrations. That fits the ""human presence"" Toshio mentioned and avoids heavy shipping.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, I agree. Local textiles would be light on the suspended bay and wouldn't be damaged by evening hire movements.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Rin,,And the town history volunteers would be perfect for a local textiles show!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Kenji,,A seems the safest. No complex electronics to break and no distant lenders to delay us.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It also avoids the bespoke mount-making fees if the garments are displayed simply. A is the most rational choice.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I feel comfortable with A. It's the most considerate of the building's limits.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Toshio,,It aligns with the visitor data. I vote for A.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Rin,,I vote for A! It's the only one that doesn't stress out the staff.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for A too. Let's actually open on time for once!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates A is the only candidate that avoids all our identified risks. I vote A.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
